@* EvidenceSettingsPage: the evidence settings of one project, at "/projects/{id}/evidence-settings". Two groups of
   switches: who may read the evidence without signing in (the evidence index and the attestation PDFs, independent
   of each other) and what every attestation PDF of the project contains (review discussion threads, reviewer names,
   checklist wording, the file list with hashes, the git context). One "Save settings" button saves all of them and a
   "Back to project" button leaves. Only whoever may administer the project (a system administrator or a project
   admin of it) gets the page; anybody else sees the not-found message of a missing project.

   Presentation only; state and event handling live in EvidenceSettingsPage.razor.cs. Each switch has a short
   description. A switch that REMOVES content from the PDFs shows a regulatory warning right below it while it is
   off, a summary notice at the top lists everything that is left out, and a distinct exposure warning shows while
   an anonymous switch is on (stronger when the PDFs still carry comments or names). All of that follows the
   choices on the page at once, before saving. Every key value carries a stable kebab-case data-testid, and the
   data-interactive marker on the root flips to "true" once the live circuit is connected.

   Human factors: (a) the settings and nothing else, anonymous access first because it is the riskiest, one save
   button; (b) each switch says what it does in one sentence and what turning it off or on costs, so nobody has to
   guess; (c) the warnings appear next to the switch that causes them and a saved change is confirmed in words.

   The page body is inside SessionGate, which replaces it with a "Session ended" message when the user is no longer
   valid while the page is open. *@
@page "/projects/{ProjectId:int}/evidence-settings"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@attribute [Authorize]

<PageTitle>Evidence settings - ReviewCenter</PageTitle>

<SessionGate>
<main class="page narrow" data-testid="evidence-settings-page" data-interactive="@InteractiveMarker">
    <nav class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/projects" data-testid="breadcrumb-projects-link">Projects</a>
        @if (Project is not null)
        {
            <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
            <a href="/projects/@ProjectId" data-testid="breadcrumb-project-link">@Project.Name</a>
            <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
            <span aria-current="page">Evidence settings</span>
        }
    </nav>

    @if (!Loaded)
    {
        <p class="muted" data-testid="evidence-settings-loading">Loading...</p>
    }
    else if (Project is null)
    {
        <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="project-not-found">Project @ProjectId does not exist.</p>
    }
    else
    {
    <h1>Evidence settings</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">Decide who may read this project's evidence and what its attestation PDFs contain.</p>

    @if (ErrorMessage is not null)
    {
        <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="evidence-settings-error">@ErrorMessage</p>
    }
    @if (StatusMessage is not null)
    {
        <p class="notice" role="status" data-testid="evidence-settings-status">@StatusMessage</p>
    }
    @if (OmittedSections.Count > 0)
    {
        <p class="notice warning" role="status" data-testid="evidence-reduced-banner">
            These choices leave out of every attestation PDF: @string.Join(", ", OmittedSections).
            Check that your regulatory regime allows it.
        </p>
    }

    <form data-testid="evidence-settings-form" @onsubmit="SaveAsync">
        <section class="card">
            <h2 class="section-title">Anonymous access</h2>
            <p class="muted hint">Both are off by default, so everything needs a sign-in or an API token.</p>
            @foreach (var item in Switches.Where(s => s.Anonymous))
            {
                <div class="field setting" data-testid="evidence-setting-@item.TestId">
                    <label class="switch">
                        <input type="checkbox" checked="@item.Get()" @onchange="e => item.Set(Checked(e))"
                               data-testid="evidence-@item.TestId-switch" />
                        @item.Title
                    </label>
                    <p class="muted hint">@item.Description</p>
                </div>
            }
            @if (AnonymousIsOn)
            {
                <p class="notice warning" data-testid="evidence-anonymous-warning">
                    Anyone who can reach this server can read what you opened, without signing in.
                    Anonymous requests are limited to @AnonymousLimit per minute per address.
                    @if (AnonymousPdfsShowPeopleOrComments)
                    {
                        <strong data-testid="evidence-anonymous-people-warning">
                            The attestation PDFs still contain @AnonymousPdfExposure; anonymous readers will see
                            them. Turn those switches off below if that is not acceptable.
                        </strong>
                    }
                </p>
            }
        </section>

        <section class="card">
            <h2 class="section-title">PDF content</h2>
            <p class="muted hint">
                These apply to every attestation PDF of this project, for sign-in and anonymous readers alike.
                Each PDF has a Content scope section that says what was left out.
            </p>
            @foreach (var item in Switches.Where(s => !s.Anonymous))
            {
                <div class="field setting" data-testid="evidence-setting-@item.TestId">
                    <label class="switch">
                        <input type="checkbox" checked="@item.Get()" @onchange="e => item.Set(Checked(e))"
                               data-testid="evidence-@item.TestId-switch" />
                        @item.Title
                    </label>
                    <p class="muted hint">@item.Description</p>
                    @if (!item.Get())
                    {
                        <p class="notice warning" data-testid="evidence-@item.TestId-warning">@item.Warning</p>
                    }
                </div>
            }
            <p class="muted hint">
                Always included: the review and project identifiers, the content fingerprint, the checklist
                outcomes, the signatures, the record digest and the signing-key note. Names typed into comments or
                other free text are not removed; only the PDF's own name fields are.
            </p>
        </section>

        <div class="plan-actions">
            <button type="submit" data-testid="evidence-settings-save">Save settings</button>
            <a class="action outline" href="/projects/@ProjectId"
               data-testid="evidence-settings-back">Back to project</a>
        </div>
    </form>
    }
</main>
</SessionGate>
